## The Chosen Path
After posting the article above, I continued thinking and working on implementing a microblog functionality into Saisho.
The route I ended up going with is probably the easiest possible implementation given the constraints and needs I have for the required functionality.

### Source File

The source file is a plain TXT file that contains all the entries in reverse order (where the newest entry is always at the top) to make it humanly readable even when looking directly at the source file.
It follows a simple structure and complies with the [twtxt](https://twtxt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user/twtxtfile.html#format-specification) format:

```
{RF3339 Date}	{Unique ID} {Flags} {Entry Text}
```
So, for example, an entry will look like

```
2020-09-26T21:17:34Z	ed58b9 P Aside from the ID and the flags (still need to figure out if I *really* need those), the format is TWTXT compatible.
```

